tvOS Browser
=============

> [!NOTE]
> **This is a continued, heavily extended version** of [jvanakker/tvOSBrowser](https://github.com/jvanakker/tvOSBrowser), which itself builds on Steven Troughton-Smith's original tvOS Browser. Compared to the upstream version it adds:
> - **Magnetic Buttons:** the pointer snaps to links and buttons, so sites built for mouse and touch work like a tvOS app
> - **Ad blocker** (uBlock Origin Lite lists, updated daily without an app update) and automatic **cookie banner** rejection
> - **Native video player** with picture in picture and **automatic subtitles** generated on the device (whisper.cpp)
> - **Page translation** with Apple's translation, done in place on the page
> - Reworked **Liquid Glass UI**, new pointer, tab management, voice commands via dictation, first-run setup
> - Interface in **English, German, Spanish and French**
>
> All changes are in the commit history: [compare with upstream](https://github.com/dennisek-lab/tvOSBrowser/compare/jvanakker:tvOSBrowser:master...main).

A web browser for Apple TV (tvOS 17 to 27) with **Magnetic Buttons**, a Liquid Glass interface, pointer control on the clickpad, ad and cookie banner blocking, a native video player, Apple's translation for web pages and automatic subtitles created on the device.

The app's interface follows the Apple TV's language: **English, German, Spanish or French** (other languages fall back to English). Menu names below are given in German with an English translation.

![Start page with Liquid Glass bar](/screen01.png?raw=true "Start page (Google) with Liquid Glass bar, pointer and glow around the search field")

![Web page with magnetic highlight](/screen02.png?raw=true "Magnetic Buttons: the pointer has snapped onto a link in the navigation bar")

![Side menu](/screen03.png?raw=true "Side menu (•••) with “Diese Seite” (This page) and “Navigation”")

The app uses **private APIs** (WebKit is loaded at runtime, translation uses private classes of Apple's Translation framework). Apple does not allow this on the App Store. It is meant for building yourself only. Please do not publish builds on the App Store. No warranty, use at your own risk.

Screenshots of the original version are in `docs/original-screens/`; licenses of third-party components are in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.


Setup
=============

There is **no** ready-made app to download. You need a Mac with Xcode (tested with Xcode 27, tvOS SDK 27.2) and an Apple TV on the same network.

1. **Pair the Apple TV once:** On the Apple TV open *Settings → Remotes and Devices → Remote App and Devices* and leave it open. In Xcode 27 choose *File → Pair Nearby Device…* in the Device Hub; the Apple TV shows a code.
2. Double-click **`Installieren.command`** in Finder. The script pulls the latest version (`git pull`), checks Xcode, downloads the whisper model if needed, builds the app, installs it and shows when the provisioning profile expires (7 days with a free Apple account, then install again).
3. Or by hand: open `_Project/Browser.xcodeproj`, scheme *Browser*, run on the Apple TV.

Script options: `--nur-bauen` (build only), `--geraete` (list Apple TVs), `--kein-pull` (skip git pull), `--debug`, `--starten`/`--nicht-starten` (launch after install or not), `UDID=…`.

**Your own team:** The project contains no team; the bundle ID is `io.github.tvosbrowser.app`. Create `_Project/Signing.local.xcconfig` (not checked in) with your own team and bundle ID:

```
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
BROWSER_BUNDLE_ID = com.example.tvbrowser
```

The team ID is shown in Xcode under *Settings → Accounts* or in your Apple Developer account. `Installieren.command` reads both values from there. Alternatively choose team and bundle ID in Xcode for the target *Browser* under *Signing & Capabilities* (the pictures are from an older Xcode, the steps are the same); this changes the checked-in project file, though.

![Change bundle ID](/readme_instruction_01.png?raw=true "Change the bundle identifier to your own")

![Change team](/readme_instruction_02.png?raw=true "Choose your own team under Signing & Capabilities")

**First launch:** A short setup walks through favorites, start page, protection (ad blocker, Cloudflare DNS, cookie banners), videos (Apple player, automatic subtitles, subtitles on web pages) and design (Liquid Glass or classic). “Überspringen” (skip) keeps the defaults (on a fresh install everything on, Liquid Glass). Then the controls guide appears. After updates “Was ist neu” (what's new) is shown once. Everything is available at any time under *••• → Hilfe* (help), the setup as “Einrichtung wiederholen”.

![First-run setup](/docs/readme-screens/ersteinrichtung.png?raw=true "Setup on first launch")


Controls
=============

| Button / gesture | Action |
|:--|:--|
| Swipe on the clickpad | Move the pointer. Magnetic Buttons: it snaps softly onto links and buttons (with glow) |
| Press the clickpad | Click |
| Press clickpad up / down | Scroll. Twice up: address bar. Twice down: shrink the bar |
| Press clickpad left / right | Jump from button to button, one press = one button; hold to keep going. Twice right: side menu (•••). In videos: skip 10 s |
| Circle on the edge | Move from element to element (also with the remote in the iPhone Control Center) |
| Play/Pause | Start/stop video, otherwise input. Hold: search and speak. Twice: side menu (•••) |
| Menu / Back | Close dialog or address bar, leave reader, then go back one page |
| Siri button, two short presses | Translate the page; two more: end translation. While the pop-up hint is showing: go to the pop-up tab. A single press does nothing |
| Hold Siri button | In the address field: dictation (address, search term or voice command) |
| TV button, volume, holding Siri outside text fields | belong to the system; apps don't receive them |

The Siri button cannot officially be read by apps. The app detects a short Siri press because tvOS reports it as a very short press to the right without a clickpad click.

**Address bar:** Pressing the bar (or twice up) opens the keyboard right below it, with favorites, frequently and recently visited sites underneath. Without another click, hold the Siri button and say an address, a search term or a **voice command** (in English, German, Spanish or French), e.g. “back”, “new tab”, “search weather”, “open heise dot de”, or in German “Reader”, “zurück” (back), “neuer Tab” (new tab), “suche Wetter” (search weather), “öffne heise punkt de” (open heise.de), “30 Sekunden zurück” (30 seconds back), “fasse zusammen” (summarize), “übersetzen” (translate), “Übersetzung beenden” (end translation).

**Text input:** For every text field the iPhone offers a keyboard notification; you can also paste passwords that way.


Features
=============

- **Magnetic Buttons:** the core of this version. The pointer is pulled onto links and buttons as soon as it gets near and holds there noticeably. It moves on to the next button only after the finger has swiped about a fifth of the clickpad width, regardless of button size and pointer speed; one change per swipe, only long, fast swipes keep going. It is released only when nothing else follows in that direction. The selected element stands out as a glass surface with a fine light edge, without magnification or refraction, framed by a soft, moving rainbow glow (static under “Glow-Animation”). The highlight hugs the element and takes its shape (pills stay pills, circles stay circles, square buttons stay square; without their own rounding iOS-style rounded). On change it pops up at the new target instead of sliding over. This way a site built for mouse and touch can be used with the clickpad like a tvOS app.
- **Interface:** bar, side menu and dialogs in Liquid Glass style (tvOS 26+), springy animations, corners following Apple's guidelines (continuous, concentric, capsules). Two-column side menu with large buttons, symbols and switches. For switches and values (page zoom, ad blocker, pointer speed …) it stays open and shows the new value; actions like new tab, favorites, translate or top bar close it. New app icons with parallax layers.
- **Classic design:** Under *••• → Ansicht & Wiedergabe → Design* you can switch to “Alt” (classic): grey bar, symbols and pointer as in the original version, without glass and Liquid Glass animations. Takes effect immediately, no restart.
- **Pointer:** own pointer pipeline (per-frame tracking, smoothing, no snapping back, short glide after a fast swipe), modern pointer images in three styles. Pointer speed in four steps; pointer acceleration (fast swipes carry further) can be turned off and is off by default.
- **Tabs:** up to ten tabs; only the five most recently used stay loaded (saves memory), the others reload on switch and return to their old position. Tab overview with previews, session restored after restart. Pop-ups and links that open a new window become background tabs; a short hint appears at the bottom right, clicking it, Play/Pause or Siri twice goes there. Tabs you never looked at close themselves after 30 minutes (can be turned off).
- **Start page:** under *••• → Navigation → Startseite festlegen* Google, a favorite, the current page or your own address; it appears when the app starts.
- **Reader mode:** articles without distraction (Readability), button left of •••.
- **Ad blocker:** uBlock Origin Lite filter lists as WebKit content rules, plus extended rules (scriptlets, procedural CSS) per site. If a site detects the blocker and locks you out (e.g. bild.de), an exception is set for that site automatically. **The lists update without an app update:** a GitHub workflow rebuilds them daily, the app fetches the new version at most once a day (checked by SHA-256, switched only after successful compilation; otherwise the previous or bundled lists stay). Status and update under *••• → Erweiterungen → Filterlisten aktualisieren*.
- **Cookie banners:** rejected automatically (autoconsent). On “accept or pay” sites it can optionally accept.
- **Page translation with Apple's translation:** The page is translated directly in the document, paragraph by paragraph, parts loaded later while scrolling. Address, cookies and login stay, forms keep working, “Übersetzung beenden” restores the original without reloading. The side menu shows the route used (“Übersetzen – Apple”). Google Translate (translate.goog) is only a fallback if Apple doesn't offer the language pair, the service is unreachable or the first section fails. On foreign-language pages a hint “Übersetzen?” appears; Play/Pause translates. Also triggered from the side menu, by voice command or Siri twice.

  ![Apple translation](/docs/readme-screens/uebersetzung-apple.png?raw=true "English Wikipedia page translated by Apple in place; the address stays en.wikipedia.org")

- **Video:** videos can be opened in the native player (picture in picture, seeking, metadata, position written back to the page), also controllable from the iPhone (Now Playing). Controls as in the TV app: click pauses, swipe up for the transport bar with subtitle, audio and “Automatische Untertitel” (automatic subtitles) menus.
- **Automatic subtitles** (local with whisper.cpp, GPU via Metal): in the native player and, through an audio tap via Web Audio, also for videos directly on the web page.
  - **Word-accurate timing:** timestamps come from whisper's DTW alignment; a subtitle starts at the first spoken word, long sentences are split at sentence ends. Measured against the official subtitles of “Tears of Steel”: median deviation 0.25 s in the simulator (English), 0.38–0.46 s on Apple TV (German).
  - **Subtitle language:** default “Automatisch” (automatic), subtitles then appear in the spoken language (detected and kept per video). Fixed choices are German, English, French, Spanish, Italian, Dutch, Polish, Turkish, Portuguese and Russian, in the player menu “Automatische Untertitel” → “Sprache” or in the side menu under “Untertitelsprache”.
  - **Translated subtitles:** If the video speaks a different language than the chosen one (e.g. English video, German subtitles), whisper transcribes in the spoken language and Apple's translation turns it into full sentences in the target language, with the previous sentence as context. Offline or on errors whisper translates by itself; live, the section then appears in the original language.

  ![Subtitles with Apple translation](/docs/ai-screens/untertitel-apple-uebersetzung.jpg?raw=true "English video (Tears of Steel), automatic subtitles in German")

- **Smart features** (local, NaturalLanguage): summarize a page, “Frag die Seite” (ask the page: the matching passage is highlighted and scrolled to, Play/Pause jumps to the next). Voice commands are also understood by meaning (“lade die Seite nochmal”, reload the page).

  ![Summary](/docs/ai-screens/zusammenfassung-heise-de.png?raw=true "Summarizing a page")

- **Voice commands:** work via dictation in the address field (see Controls). App Shortcuts for Siri (“Starte den Reader in tvOS Browser”) are built in, see limitations.
- **DNS via Cloudflare** (DoH) for the web view, can be turned off.


Settings (•••)
=============

| Section | Entries |
|:--|:--|
| Diese Seite (this page) | Summarize, translate or end translation (route “Apple” or “Google”), reload, page zoom, ad blocker here, reject cookie banners here |
| Navigation | Open start page, set start page, favorites, history, show tabs, new tab, close unused tabs after 30 min |
| Erweiterungen (extensions) | Ad blocker, pause ad blocker automatically when locked out, update filter lists (with status), reject cookie banners, accept paywalls, native player automatically, automatic subtitles, subtitle language (automatic, German, English, French, Spanish, Italian, Dutch, Polish, Turkish, Portuguese, Russian), subtitles (web page), Cloudflare DNS |
| Ansicht & Wiedergabe (view & playback) | Top bar, rainbow glow, design (Liquid Glass/classic), glow animation (off: static gradient; always static with “Reduce Motion”), Liquid Glass animations, pointer (dark/light/symbol), pointer speed (slow/normal/fast/very fast), pointer acceleration (off by default), pointer glide, full-screen player, fit page to width, user agent (desktop/mobile), font larger/smaller/reset |
| Daten (data) | Clear cache, delete cookies |
| Hilfe (help) | Repeat setup, controls, what's new |
| Erweitert (advanced) | Media diagnostics, WebKit media settings |

Switches and values keep the side menu open; entries that navigate or open a dialog close it.


Notes and known limitations
=============

- **Private APIs:** Any tvOS update can break something. Reinstall the app and go through the checklist in `docs/ERWEITERUNGEN.md` (section 2).
- **No App Store**; with a free account the profile expires after 7 days.
- **DRM videos** (Netflix and the like) don't play; subtitles on web pages don't work with DRM, native HLS or third-party servers without CORS.
- **Passkeys** are not supported; password logins work.
- **Apple Intelligence:** Foundation Models, Writing Tools and the public Translation API are blocked for apps on tvOS. Summaries therefore use NaturalLanguage and are simpler (extractive). Translation uses private classes of the Translation framework, online only via Apple's servers (offline models can't be loaded from the app); without network Google steps in for pages and whisper for subtitles. On Apple's route Apple's servers get the text and Google doesn't see the page; only the translate.goog fallback loads the page through Google (without the original site's cookies and login).
- **Siri** on Apple TV doesn't trigger custom phrases of third-party apps, so the App Shortcuts have no effect there. Voice commands work via dictation.
- Whisper models (`_Project/Browser/WhisperModels/*.bin`) are not in the repo; `Installieren.command` or `tools/fetch_whisper_model.sh` downloads them.


